From 4ac8a9e7142e63a2fe6c63e110132c4a06c88d75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:49:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 104/104] R1's consumption capture: a named draw's inputs,
 state and output, as the GPU used them

Development only, off unless DOTHEROES_R1_DIR, DOTHEROES_R1_AT and
DOTHEROES_R1_DRAWS are set (docs/NATIVE_PORT.md section 5 of the port).

- The engine (rsx_draw_engine.c) names draws by colour target offset,
  fragment program offset and occurrence in the frame, in the first frame
  after DOTHEROES_R1_AT seconds. For one, it makes the programs' HLSL again
  (eng_programs_text) with the microcode it read after every queued write
  had landed, and hands the backend a description (rsx_be_capture, the
  backend's new optional capture_next_draw).
- The Vulkan backend (rsx_vulkan_backend.c): before the draw everything is
  submitted and waited for, and each bound texture and the colour target
  copied to host memory; the draw is recorded as always and what it binds
  written down as Vulkan values (vk_eng_variant_info's create info,
  constants, vertices, viewport, scissor, dynamic state); after it, it is
  submitted and the target copied again: the reference output. Into
  <dir>/<name>/desc.json (native terms only) and the files it names.
- Each pipeline keeps a hash of the HLSL it was made from; the capture says
  whether the text it made again is that text (programs_match_pipeline).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
